{"id":"word:hebrew:H3123","type":"word","title":"יוֹנָה","subtitle":"H3123 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a dove (apparently from the warmth of their mating)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יוֹנָה (H3123) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 33 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יוֹנָה (yôwnâh) means a dove (apparently from the warmth of their mating) First listed occurrence: 2Kgs 6 25."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יוֹנָה","transliteration":"yôwnâh","pronunciation":"yo-naw'","strong":"H3123","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3123","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["הַ/יּוֹנָ֖ה","יוֹנָ֑ה","וְ/כַ/יּוֹנִ֖ים","יוֹנָ֔ה","יוֹנִ֔ים"],"morphs":[["HNcfsa",9],["HTd/Ncfsa",7],["HNcfpa",4],["HNcfsc/Sp1cs",3],["HR/Ncfsa",2],["HRd/Ncfsa",2],["HC/Rd/Ncfpa",2],["HR/Ncfpc",1],["HC/R/Ncfsa",1],["HNcfsc",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a dove (apparently from the warmth of their mating)","usage":"dove, pigeon.","full":"H3123. yonah I. יוֺנָה noun feminine dove (Late Hebrew id. ; Aramaic id. , ) — absolute יוֺנָה Gen 8:8 20 t.; construct יוֺנֵת Psa 56:1 ; suffix יוֺנָתִי Song 2:14 2 t.; plural יוֺנִים Nahum 2:8 6 t.; construct יוֺנֵי Ezek 7:16 (see below); — dove Gen 8:8-9 , 10 , 11 , 12 (all J); often of offerings, בֶּןיֿוֺנָה Lev 12:6 (P; an individual of the species; || תֹּר ); (ה)יוֺנִים בְּנֵי || תֹּרִיםׅ 1:14 ; 5:7 , 11 ; 12:8 ; 14:22 , 30 ; 15:14 , 29 ; Num 6:10 (all P); יוֺנִים חֲרִי dove's dung 2Kin 6:25 (Kt, yet see Gei Urschrift 409 ); in various similes: Ephraim is מּוֺתָה כְּיוֺנָה like a silly dove Hosea 7:11 (allowing itself to be snared); simile of return of exiles, like eager flight of doves 11:11 , of ships with white outspread sails Isa 60:8 ; כַּיּוֺנָה אֵבֶר Psa 55:7 ; see also יוֺנָה כַּנְפֵי 68:14 ; simile of fugitive Moab Jer 48:28 ; also הַגֵּאָיוֺת כְּיוֺנֵי Ezek 7:16 like the doves of the valleys (but on text see Co, who emends הוֺגִיּוֺת כיונים , but regards phrase as gloss): simile of mourning יוֺנִים כְּקוֺל Nahum 2:8 ; without כיונים הגה קוֺל, Isa 38:14 ; 59:11 (from mournful note); figurative of beauty (only Canticles): יוֺנִים עֵינַיִךְ thine eyes are (those of) doves Song 1:15 ; 4:1 , see also 4:12 ; term of endearment, יוֺנָתִי my dove 2:14 ; 5:2 ; 6:9 . Elsewhere only Psa 56:1 (title) רְחֹקִים אֵלֶם יוֺנַת (עַל) probably name of melody: To 'the dove of distant terebinths' (read אֵלִים for אֵלֶם ; see אֵלֶם above, and Bae Psalms, p. xvii ). — On sanctity of dove among Shemites, see RS Semitic i. 202, 275 .","rootNote":"probably from the same as 3196 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Kgs 6 25","keyReferences":["2Kgs 6 25","Ezek 7 16","Gen 8 8","Gen 8 9","Gen 8 10","Gen 8 11","Gen 8 12","Hos 7 11"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":33,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Kgs 6 25","book":"2Kgs","chapter":6,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יונים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfpa"},{"reference":"Ezek 7 16","book":"Ezek","chapter":7,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כְּ/יוֹנֵ֧י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncfpc"},{"reference":"Gen 8 8","book":"Gen","chapter":8,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/יּוֹנָ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"Gen 8 9","book":"Gen","chapter":8,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/יּוֹנָ֨ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"Gen 8 10","book":"Gen","chapter":8,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/יּוֹנָ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"Gen 8 11","book":"Gen","chapter":8,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/יּוֹנָה֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"Gen 8 12","book":"Gen","chapter":8,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/יּוֹנָ֔ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"Hos 7 11","book":"Ho